## Architecture Diagram

Below is a diagram of an example e-commerce analytics pipeline. I created this diagram to demonstrate my understanding of how data flows from source systems to executive dashboards.

![Data Pipeline Architecture Diagram](./Architecture Diagram - E-commerce Analytics Pipeline.png)

### Diagram Legend

| Color | Layer | Purpose |
|-------|-------|---------|
| Blue | Source Systems | Where raw data originates |
| Green | Ingestion | Scheduled extraction of data |
| Yellow | Raw Storage | Immutable staging area |
| Orange | Transformation | Cleaning and business logic |
| Purple | Warehouse & BI | Reporting and visualization |
| Red | Monitoring | Monitor for success or failure |

### Tools Represented

- PostgreSQL – Transactional database
- Google Analytics – Web analytics
- Facebook Ads – Marketing data
- Azure Data Factory – Orchestration
- Azure Blob Storage – Raw storage
- Azure Synapse / dbt – Transformation
- Snowflake – Data warehouse
- Power BI – Dashboards

### What This Diagram Shows

This pipeline extracts data daily from three source systems, stages it in blob storage, transforms it using SQL-based logic, loads it into Snowflake, and finally refreshes a Power BI dashboard for executives. The entire process is orchestrated by Azure Data Factory and monitored for failures.
